# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug/
target/
reference/

# Trunk build output
dist/

# Node dependencies and local Cloudflare Worker state. The Worker lives in
# `worker/`, which is where wrangler and miniflare are installed: those packages,
# the state and cache they write while developing, and the secrets file they read
# are all local. The Worker's own files, if any, are still worth committing.
node_modules/
.wrangler/
.dev.vars*
!.dev.vars.example

# Python userbot (userbot/): bytecode, local env files and session strings.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
userbot/.env
userbot/*.env
!userbot/userbot.env.example
userbot/*.session

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/